@title: Tiếng Anh Du lịch
@author: Thực hành theo tình huống
@lang: vi

# Cách dùng sách này

Du lịch khác công việc ở một điểm: bạn hầu như luôn nói chuyện với **người lạ đang bận**. Nhân viên sân bay, lễ tân, tài xế — họ nghe hàng trăm người mỗi ngày. Câu ngắn và rõ hiệu quả hơn câu đúng ngữ pháp nhưng dài.

Sách này ưu tiên những câu bạn dùng được ngay. Học thuộc mười câu trong một chương còn hơn hiểu lơ mơ cả trăm câu.

> Một mẹo đáng giá: khi không nghe rõ, đừng gật đầu. Nói **Sorry?** rồi nghe lại. Gật bừa là cách nhanh nhất để lên nhầm chuyến hoặc trả nhầm tiền.

# Chương 1 — Sân bay

## Từ vựng

@vocab
boarding pass | /ˈbɔːdɪŋ pɑːs/ | thẻ lên máy bay | Please have your boarding pass ready.
check in | /tʃek ɪn/ | làm thủ tục | Where do I check in for Bangkok?
carry-on | /ˈkæri ɒn/ | hành lý xách tay | Is this small enough as a carry-on?
checked baggage | /tʃekt ˈbæɡɪdʒ/ | hành lý ký gửi | One piece of checked baggage, please.
aisle seat | /aɪl siːt/ | ghế cạnh lối đi | Could I have an aisle seat?
window seat | /ˈwɪndəʊ siːt/ | ghế cạnh cửa sổ | I'd prefer a window seat.
gate | /ɡeɪt/ | cửa ra máy bay | The gate has changed to B12.
layover | /ˈleɪəʊvə/ | thời gian chờ nối chuyến | I have a four-hour layover in Doha.
connecting flight | /kəˈnektɪŋ flaɪt/ | chuyến nối | Will I make my connecting flight?
delayed | /dɪˈleɪd/ | bị hoãn | The flight is delayed by two hours.
customs | /ˈkʌstəmz/ | hải quan | Do I go through customs here?
declare | /dɪˈkleə/ | khai báo | I have nothing to declare.
@end

## Mẫu câu

- **Where do I check in for flight VN310?**
- **Could I have an aisle seat, please?**
- **Is this within the carry-on size limit?**
- **How much is the excess baggage fee?**
- **Which gate is it boarding from?**
- **I have a connecting flight. Will my bag go through?**
- **My flight was cancelled. What are my options?**
- **Is there a later flight today?**
- **Where can I find the transfer desk?**
- **My luggage didn't arrive. Where do I report it?**

## Hội thoại mẫu

@dialog
Agent: Good morning. Where are you flying today?
Thuan: Singapore, on flight SQ179.
Agent: Passport and any bags to check?
Thuan: Here's my passport. One bag to check, and this as carry-on.
Agent: That's fine. Would you like a window or an aisle seat?
Thuan: Aisle, please. And I have a connection in Singapore.
Agent: To where?
Thuan: Sydney, three hours later.
Agent: I'll tag your bag through to Sydney. You won't need to collect it.
Thuan: That's helpful, thanks. Which gate?
Agent: B14, boarding at ten past nine. It's a fifteen-minute walk.
@end

## Khi có sự cố

- **My flight was cancelled. Can you rebook me?**
- **I've been waiting two hours. Is there any update?**
- **Am I entitled to compensation?**
- **Could you write that down for me?**
- **Is there someone who speaks Vietnamese?**

# Chương 2 — Khách sạn

## Từ vựng

@vocab
reservation | /ˌrezəˈveɪʃn/ | đặt phòng | I have a reservation under Nguyen.
check-in time | /ˈtʃek ɪn taɪm/ | giờ nhận phòng | What time is check-in?
check out | /tʃek aʊt/ | trả phòng | I'd like to check out, please.
vacancy | /ˈveɪkənsi/ | phòng trống | Do you have any vacancies tonight?
en suite | /ˌɒn ˈswiːt/ | có phòng tắm riêng | Is the room en suite?
amenities | /əˈmenətiz/ | tiện nghi | The amenities include a gym and pool.
housekeeping | /ˈhaʊskiːpɪŋ/ | dọn phòng | Could housekeeping come after noon?
deposit | /dɪˈpɒzɪt/ | tiền đặt cọc | Is a deposit required?
late checkout | /leɪt ˈtʃekaʊt/ | trả phòng muộn | Is late checkout possible?
complimentary | /ˌkɒmplɪˈmentri/ | miễn phí kèm theo | Breakfast is complimentary.
@end

## Mẫu câu

- **I have a reservation under the name Nguyen.**
- **Is breakfast included in the rate?**
- **Could I get a room on a higher floor?**
- **The room next door is very noisy. Could I move?**
- **The air conditioning isn't working.**
- **Could you store my luggage until my flight?**
- **Is there a laundry service?**
- **Could I have a late checkout? My flight is at eight.**
- **Could you call me a taxi for six in the morning?**
- **Could I have the bill, please? I think there's a mistake.**

## Hội thoại mẫu

@dialog
Thuan: Good evening. I have a reservation under Nguyen.
Clerk: Let me check. Three nights, a double room?
Thuan: That's right. Is breakfast included?
Clerk: It is, from six thirty to ten in the restaurant on the ground floor.
Thuan: Great. Is there a quieter room available? I'm a light sleeper.
Clerk: I can move you to the fifth floor, away from the road.
Thuan: That would be perfect. One more thing — what time is checkout?
Clerk: Noon. Late checkout until two is possible for a small fee.
Thuan: I may need that. I'll let you know tomorrow.
@end

# Chương 3 — Nhà hàng và quán ăn

## Từ vựng

@vocab
book a table | /bʊk ə ˈteɪbl/ | đặt bàn | I'd like to book a table for four.
starter | /ˈstɑːtə/ | món khai vị | What do you recommend as a starter?
main course | /meɪn kɔːs/ | món chính | I'll have the fish as a main course.
side dish | /saɪd dɪʃ/ | món ăn kèm | Could I get a side of rice?
rare | /reə/ | tái | Medium rare, please.
well done | /wel dʌn/ | chín kỹ | I'd like it well done.
allergic | /əˈlɜːdʒɪk/ | dị ứng | I'm allergic to peanuts.
vegetarian | /ˌvedʒɪˈteəriən/ | ăn chay | Do you have vegetarian options?
the bill | /ðə bɪl/ | hoá đơn | Could we have the bill, please?
split the bill | /splɪt ðə bɪl/ | chia tiền | Shall we split the bill?
tip | /tɪp/ | tiền boa | Is service included, or should I tip?
takeaway | /ˈteɪkəweɪ/ | mang về | Can I get this as a takeaway?
@end

## Mẫu câu

- **A table for two, please.**
- **Do you have a table by the window?**
- **What would you recommend?**
- **What's in this dish?**
- **I'm allergic to shellfish. Does this contain any?**
- **Could I have that without chilli?**
- **Is this spicy?**
- **Could we have some more water, please?**
- **This isn't what I ordered.**
- **Could we have the bill, please?**
- **Is service included?**
- **Do you take card?**

> Câu **I'm allergic to...** đáng học thuộc chính xác. Nói *I don't eat...* thì bếp có thể coi là sở thích, nhưng *allergic* thì họ xử lý nghiêm túc.

## Hội thoại mẫu

@dialog
Waiter: Good evening. Do you have a reservation?
Thuan: No, we don't. A table for two, if possible?
Waiter: We have one by the window. Will that do?
Thuan: That's perfect, thank you. Could we see the menu?
Waiter: Of course. Today's special is the grilled sea bass.
Thuan: That sounds good. Does it come with anything?
Waiter: Roast vegetables and potatoes.
Thuan: I'll take that. One thing — I'm allergic to shellfish. Is the sauce safe?
Waiter: Let me check with the kitchen to be sure.
Thuan: I'd appreciate it, thanks.
@end

# Chương 4 — Đi lại và hỏi đường

## Từ vựng

@vocab
one way | /wʌn weɪ/ | một chiều | One way to the airport, please.
return ticket | /rɪˈtɜːn ˈtɪkɪt/ | vé khứ hồi | A return ticket to Oxford, please.
platform | /ˈplætfɔːm/ | sân ga | Which platform for the London train?
fare | /feə/ | giá vé | What's the fare to the city centre?
change | /tʃeɪndʒ/ | đổi tuyến; tiền thối | Do I need to change trains?
stop | /stɒp/ | điểm dừng | How many stops is it?
get off | /ɡet ɒf/ | xuống xe | Where should I get off?
straight ahead | /streɪt əˈhed/ | đi thẳng | Go straight ahead for two blocks.
turn left | /tɜːn left/ | rẽ trái | Turn left at the traffic lights.
around the corner | /əˈraʊnd ðə ˈkɔːnə/ | ngay góc phố | It's just around the corner.
opposite | /ˈɒpəzɪt/ | đối diện | It's opposite the bank.
on foot | /ɒn fʊt/ | đi bộ | Is it walkable on foot?
@end

## Mẫu câu

- **How do I get to the old town from here?**
- **Is it within walking distance?**
- **Which platform does the train to Oxford leave from?**
- **Does this bus go to the museum?**
- **Could you tell me when to get off?**
- **How much is the fare?**
- **Could you use the meter, please?**
- **I'd like to go to this address.** (đưa điện thoại ra cho tài xế xem)
- **Could you stop here, please?**
- **Keep the change.**
- **I think we're going the wrong way.**

## Hội thoại mẫu

@dialog
Thuan: Excuse me, how do I get to the National Museum?
Local: You can walk. It's about fifteen minutes.
Thuan: Could you show me on the map?
Local: Sure. Go straight ahead to the big square, then turn left.
Thuan: Straight, then left at the square.
Local: That's it. The museum is opposite a large church. You can't miss it.
Thuan: And if I take the bus instead?
Local: Number 12, from that stop. Three stops, then it's a short walk.
Thuan: Thank you very much. You've been very helpful.
@end

# Chương 5 — Mua sắm

## Từ vựng

@vocab
browse | /braʊz/ | xem lướt qua | I'm just browsing, thanks.
try on | /traɪ ɒn/ | mặc thử | Could I try this on?
fitting room | /ˈfɪtɪŋ ruːm/ | phòng thử đồ | Where's the fitting room?
in stock | /ɪn stɒk/ | còn hàng | Do you have this in stock?
sold out | /səʊld aʊt/ | hết hàng | The medium is sold out.
receipt | /rɪˈsiːt/ | hoá đơn | Keep the receipt for returns.
refund | /ˈriːfʌnd/ | hoàn tiền | Can I get a refund?
exchange | /ɪksˈtʃeɪndʒ/ | đổi hàng | Could I exchange this for a larger size?
bargain | /ˈbɑːɡɪn/ | mặc cả; món hời | It was a real bargain.
haggle | /ˈhæɡl/ | mặc cả | You're expected to haggle at this market.
@end

## Mẫu câu

- **I'm just looking, thanks.**
- **Do you have this in a medium?**
- **Do you have this in another colour?**
- **Could I try this on?**
- **How much is this?**
- **That's a bit more than I wanted to spend.**
- **Is there a discount if I take two?**
- **Can I pay by card?**
- **Could I have a receipt, please?**
- **Can I return this if it doesn't fit?**

## Mặc cả

Ở chợ châu Á, Trung Đông, Bắc Phi thì mặc cả là bình thường. Ở cửa hàng có niêm yết giá thì không.

- **What's your best price?**
- **Would you take five hundred?**
- **That's too much for me. Thanks anyway.** — rồi bước đi. Đây là câu hiệu quả nhất.

# Chương 6 — Tình huống khẩn cấp

Chương này ngắn nhưng quan trọng nhất. Học thuộc, đừng chỉ đọc.

## Từ vựng

@vocab
emergency | /ɪˈmɜːdʒənsi/ | tình huống khẩn | This is an emergency.
ambulance | /ˈæmbjələns/ | xe cứu thương | Please call an ambulance.
pharmacy | /ˈfɑːməsi/ | hiệu thuốc | Where's the nearest pharmacy?
prescription | /prɪˈskrɪpʃn/ | đơn thuốc | Do I need a prescription for this?
symptom | /ˈsɪmptəm/ | triệu chứng | My symptoms started yesterday.
painkiller | /ˈpeɪnkɪlə/ | thuốc giảm đau | Could I get some painkillers?
insurance | /ɪnˈʃʊərəns/ | bảo hiểm | I have travel insurance.
stolen | /ˈstəʊlən/ | bị đánh cắp | My wallet was stolen.
embassy | /ˈembəsi/ | đại sứ quán | I need to contact my embassy.
report | /rɪˈpɔːt/ | trình báo | I'd like to report a theft.
@end

## Mẫu câu

- **I need help.**
- **Please call an ambulance.**
- **Is there a doctor nearby?**
- **I'm allergic to penicillin.**
- **I have a fever and a bad headache.**
- **My passport was stolen. Where's the police station?**
- **I'd like to report a theft. I need a written report for my insurance.**
- **I need to contact the Vietnamese embassy.**
- **I've lost my phone. Is there a lost property office?**
- **Could you speak more slowly, please?**

> Trước khi đi, lưu sẵn vào điện thoại: số điện thoại đại sứ quán Việt Nam tại nước đó, số bảo hiểm du lịch, và ảnh chụp hộ chiếu. Ba thứ này cứu bạn khi mất hết đồ.

# Chương 7 — Trò chuyện xã giao

Người phương Tây trò chuyện với người lạ nhiều hơn ta tưởng — trên tàu, trong hàng chờ, ở quán bar. Vài câu đơn giản làm chuyến đi khác hẳn.

## Chủ đề an toàn

- Thời tiết, chuyến đi, đồ ăn, thể thao, phim ảnh.
- **Where are you from?** / **Is this your first time here?**
- **How long are you staying?**
- **What have you seen so far?**
- **Any recommendations for a good local place to eat?**

## Chủ đề nên tránh

Tiền lương, tuổi tác, cân nặng, tình trạng hôn nhân, chính trị, tôn giáo. Ở Việt Nam hỏi tuổi là bình thường; ở phương Tây thì không.

## Mẫu câu

- **I'm from Vietnam — Hanoi, in the north.**
- **This is my first time in Europe.**
- **The food here is amazing. What's this dish called?**
- **Do you know anywhere good for coffee?**
- **It was nice talking to you. Enjoy your trip.**

## Hội thoại mẫu

@dialog
Stranger: Beautiful day, isn't it?
Thuan: It really is. Much warmer than I expected.
Stranger: You're not from here?
Thuan: No, I'm from Vietnam. First time in Portugal.
Stranger: How are you finding it?
Thuan: Wonderful. Though I wasn't ready for dinner at ten at night.
Stranger: Ha, yes. We eat late here. Have you tried the seafood?
Thuan: Not yet. Anywhere you'd recommend?
Stranger: There's a small place behind the market. No sign, blue door. Best in town.
Thuan: A place with no sign — that's usually a good sign. Thank you.
@end
